# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 246-253 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 2, 2026-09-26): the father's wife and the kin of the raped
# (246); the crushed and the cut, the eunuch of the sun, the four assemblies (247); the mamzer (the one of impaired lineage) by three definitions and the tenth
# generation's analogy (248); Ammon and Moab — males not females, the two arguments and the free word (249); the counsel, Balaam's compliment and the curser
# cursed (250); no peace and no good for them (251); Edom and Egypt, the reward of an unmeant kindness, the seducer worse than the killer (252); sons and not
# daughters, R. Shimon's tradition, the third generation and Benjamin the proselyte (253). Every row READ WHOLE in both files (the whole-row rule); the cuts
# by ch22_ink.SP_ (the misses collected). Sitting 16's form; RUN 1's five files the precedent.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(246, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"A MAN SHALL NOT TAKE HIS FATHER\'S WIFE" (23:1) — HENCE: ONE MARRIES THE KIN OF A WOMAN HE RAPED OR SEDUCED, BUT THE RAPIST OR SEDUCER OF A MARRIED WOMAN\'S KIN IS LIABLE; A MAN MARRIES THE WOMAN HIS FATHER OR HIS SON RAPED OR SEDUCED; R. JUDAH FORBIDS HIS FATHER\'S. The head row of piska 246 — the chapter\'s first verse, the English Bible\'s 22:30 ({SP_(246, 1, "נושאים", "על", "האנוסה", "ועל", "המפותה")} "one marries the kin of the raped and the seduced"; {SP_(246, 1, "והאונס", "והמפתה", "על", "הנשואה", "חיב")} "the rapist and the seducer of the married woman\'s kin is liable"; {SP_(246, 1, "רבי", "יהודה", "אוסר")} "R. Judah forbids"): THE FATHER\'S WIFE the marriage (Leviticus 18:8\'s twin), not the rape — a rape makes no kinship; Yevamot 11:1 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=", the Hebrew cites no tractate). Fresh.')
srow(247, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONE WITH A CRUSHING WOUND SHALL NOT ENTER" (23:2) — WHAT IS THE CRUSHED? ANY WHOSE TESTICLES WERE WOUNDED, EVEN ONE OF THEM; ONLY ALL OF THEM? WHENCE EVEN PART? THE TEACHING SAYS "CRUSHED". The head row of piska 247 ({SP_(247, 1, "איזהו", "פצוע", "דכא")} "what is one with a crushing wound?"; {SP_(247, 1, "שנפצעו", "הביצים", "שלו")} "whose testicles were wounded"; {SP_(247, 1, "ואפלו", "אחת", "מהן")} "even one of them"): THE CLASS DEFINED by the organ and widened to a part — Yevamot 8:2 the answer sheet\'s row; the compile\'s status on a class of persons (the design\'s (c)). Fresh.')
srow(247, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ONE WITH A SEVERED MEMBER" — ANY WHOSE MEMBER IS CUT. ({SP_(247, 2, "שנכרת", "הגיד")} "whose member is cut"): the second class of 23:2; Yevamot 8:2 again. Fresh.')
srow(247, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ISHMAEL B. R. YOHANAN B. BEROKA: I HEARD IN THE VINEYARD AT YAVNEH — ONE WITH ONLY ONE TESTICLE IS A EUNUCH OF THE SUN (BORN SO); THE CRUSHED MAY HEAL, THE SEVERED NEVER — THE HEALERS\' TRADITION. ({SP_(247, 3, "שמעתי", "בכרם", "ביבנה")} "I heard in the vineyard at Yavneh"; {SP_(247, 3, "סריס", "חמה")} "a eunuch of the sun"; {SP_(247, 3, "זו", "הלכת", "רופאים")} "this is the healers\' tradition"): the two classes told apart by prognosis — a PARAMETER the physicians supply, not the verse; the congenital eunuch a third class outside the verse. Fresh.')
srow(247, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"INTO THE ASSEMBLY OF THE LORD" — R. JUDAH: FOUR ASSEMBLIES — PRIESTS, LEVITES, ISRAEL, PROSELYTES. ({SP_(247, 4, "ארבע", "קהלות", "הן")} "there are four assemblies"; {SP_(247, 4, "קהל", "גרים")} "the assembly of proselytes"): the assembly of the LORD (find 8\'s four seats, all here) partitioned — R. Judah\'s four. Fresh.')
srow(247, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'THE SAGES SAY: THREE. ({SP_(247, 5, "וחכמים", "אומרים", "שלש")} "and the sages say: three"): the proselytes no assembly of their own — the crushed proselyte may marry a proselyte woman (Kiddushin 4:1 the English\'s "cf."); a disputed PARAMETER on the classes. Fresh.')
srow(248, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO MAMZER SHALL ENTER THE ASSEMBLY OF THE LORD" (23:3) — MAN OR WOMAN; "NO MAMZER" — WHOEVER IS ONE. The head row of piska 248 ({SP_(248, 1, "בין", "איש", "בין", "אשה")} "whether man or woman"; {SP_(248, 1, "כל", "שהוא", "ממזר")} "anyone who is a mamzer"): the status on both sexes — 249:2-3\'s argument turns on it; the English\'s "defiling blemish" (mum zar) the translator\'s play on the word. Fresh.')
srow(248, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'WHAT IS A MAMZER? ANY NEAR KIN UNDER "SHALL NOT ENTER" — R. AKIVA; FOR 23:1 AND 23:3 STAND TOGETHER: AS THE FATHER\'S WIFE IS NEAR KIN UNDER THE BAN AND HER CHILD A MAMZER, SO EVERY NEAR KIN UNDER THE BAN. ({SP_(248, 2, "איזהו", "ממזר")} "what is a mamzer?"; {SP_(248, 2, "כל", "שאר", "בשר")} "any near kin"; {SP_(248, 2, "דברי", "רבי", "עקיבה")} "words of R. Akiva"; {SP_(248, 2, "מה", "אשת", "אב", "מיוחדת")} "just as the father\'s wife is distinctive"): THE FIRST OF THREE DEFINITIONS — the widest, by the verses\' adjacency (23:1 beside 23:3); Yevamot 4:13 the answer sheet\'s three-way row. Fresh.')
srow(248, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'SHIMON THE TEMANITE: ANY UNION LIABLE TO EXCISION BY HEAVEN — THE CHILD A MAMZER; THE FATHER\'S WIFE THE PROTOTYPE. ({SP_(248, 3, "שמעון", "התימני", "אומר")} "Shimon the Temanite says"; {SP_(248, 3, "כרת", "בידי", "שמים")} "excision by the hand of Heaven"; {SP_(248, 3, "הולד", "ממזר")} "the child is a mamzer"): the second definition — the sanction the class\'s key; the same prototype argument with a narrower predicate. Fresh.')
srow(248, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JOSHUA: ANY UNION LIABLE TO DEATH BY THE COURT — THE CHILD A MAMZER. ({SP_(248, 4, "רבי", "יהושע", "אומר")} "R. Joshua says"; {SP_(248, 4, "מיתת", "בית", "דין")} "death by the court"; {SP_(248, 4, "הולד", "ממזר")} "the child is a mamzer"): the third and narrowest — THREE PARAMETERS for one status, the answer sheet\'s dispute (Yevamot 4:13) carried whole in the spine; the compile\'s status takes the sanction class as its argument. Fresh.')
srow(248, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE TENTH GENERATION" — SAID HERE (23:3) AND SAID THERE (23:4); AS THERE IT MEANS FOR EVER, SO HERE FOR EVER. ({SP_(248, 5, "נאמר", "כאן", "דור", "עשירי")} "it is said here \'the tenth generation\'"; {SP_(248, 5, "ונאמר", "להלן", "דור", "עשירי")} "and said there \'the tenth generation\'"; {SP_(248, 5, "עד", "עולם")} "for ever"): THE VERBAL ANALOGY (the shared words 23:3 and 23:4, find 8\'s run of seven) — the mamzer\'s ban permanent though the verse says ten; the ordinal the parser read [10] at both seats made a COUNT that never ends. Fresh.')
srow(249, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO AMMONITE OR MOABITE SHALL ENTER" (23:4) — SCRIPTURE SPEAKS OF MALES, NOT FEMALES: AMMONITE NOT AMMONITESS, MOABITE NOT MOABITESS — R. JUDAH; THE SAGES: "BECAUSE THEY MET YOU NOT WITH BREAD AND WATER" — WHOSE WAY IS IT TO GO OUT TO MEET? MEN, NOT WOMEN. The head row of piska 249 ({SP_(249, 1, "בזכרים", "הכתוב", "מדבר", "ולא", "בנקבות")} "Scripture speaks of males and not of females"; {SP_(249, 1, "עמוני", "ולא", "עמונית")} "an Ammonite and not an Ammonitess"; {SP_(249, 1, "מי", "דרכו", "לקדם")} "whose way is it to go out to meet?"; {SP_(249, 1, "אנשים", "ולא", "נשים")} "men and not women"): THE SEX PARAMETER of the ban — two grounds for one verdict (the noun\'s gender; the reason\'s deed); Ruth the Moabitess the tape\'s own case to come; Yevamot 8:3 the answer sheet. Fresh.')
srow(249, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR IT MIGHT HAVE BEEN ARGUED: THE MAMZER, OF WHOM "FOR EVER" IS NOT SAID, HAS WOMEN AS MEN — AMMON AND MOAB, OF WHOM IT IS SAID, ALL THE MORE? OR THE REVERSE. THE TEACHING SAYS "NO MAMZER" — MAN OR WOMAN. ({SP_(249, 2, "שהיה", "בדין")} "for it might have been argued"; {SP_(249, 2, "נשים", "כאנשים")} "women as men"; {SP_(249, 2, "או", "חלוף")} "or the reverse"; {SP_(249, 2, "בין", "איש", "בין", "אשה")} "whether man or woman"): the two a fortiori arguments that cancel — the verse\'s words decide (248:1\'s "man or woman" for the mamzer). Fresh.')
srow(249, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'AFTER SCRIPTURE WIDENED IT NARROWED — ARGUE ONLY AS THE FIRST ARGUMENT; THE TEACHING SAYS "AMMONITE" AND NOT AMMONITESS — R. JUDAH. ({SP_(249, 3, "אחר", "שרבה", "הכתוב", "מיעט")} "after Scripture widened, it narrowed"; {SP_(249, 3, "כדין", "הראשון")} "as the first argument"; {SP_(249, 3, "דברי", "רבי", "יהודה")} "words of R. Judah"): the resolution — the mamzer\'s women in, Ammon\'s and Moab\'s women out, each by its verse\'s own word. Fresh.')
srow(249, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'IF "THE TENTH GENERATION" IS SAID, WHY "FOR EVER"? A FREE WORD TO COMPARE AND ARGUE A VERBAL ANALOGY: THE TENTH GENERATION HERE (23:4) IS FOR EVER, SO THE TENTH GENERATION ABOVE (23:3). ({SP_(249, 4, "מופנה", "להקיש", "ולדון", "גזרה", "שוה")} "free to compare and to argue a verbal analogy (gezerah shavah)"): THE ANALOGY\'S LICENSE named in the Hebrew — the redundant "for ever" the free word (mufneh) that permits 248:5\'s inference; the shelf\'s own method row. Fresh.')
srow(250, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BECAUSE THEY MET YOU NOT WITH BREAD AND WATER" (23:5) — "BECAUSE OF THE WORD": ALSO FOR THE COUNSEL; SO MICAH 6:5 "REMEMBER WHAT BALAK KING OF MOAB COUNSELED". The head row of piska 250 ({SP_(250, 1, "אף", "על", "העצה")} "also for the counsel"; {SP_(250, 1, "מה", "יעץ", "בלק", "מלך", "מואב")} "what Balak king of Moab counseled"): the ban\'s ground doubled — the bread withheld and Balak\'s counsel (Numbers 22-24 on the tape, the RUN CITATION behind); Micah the Prophets\' receipt of the same; the design\'s DV23-01. Fresh.')
srow(250, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"ON THE WAY" — IN THE HOUR OF YOUR CONFUSION. ({SP_(250, 2, "בשעת", "טרופכם")} "in the hour of your confusion"): the phrase of the three remembrances (find 2) glossed — the wilderness\'s distress. Fresh.')
srow(250, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHEN YOU CAME OUT OF EGYPT" — IN THE HOUR OF YOUR REDEMPTION. ({SP_(250, 3, "בשעת", "גאלתכם")} "in the hour of your redemption"): the exodus the hour; the English\'s cross-reference to 275 (Miriam, 24:9) — the same phrase\'s next seat. Fresh.')
srow(250, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND BECAUSE HE HIRED BALAAM SON OF BEOR AGAINST YOU" — A THING OF BEAUTY TO BALAAM. ({SP_(250, 4, "הרי", "דבר", "נוי", "לבלעם")} "a thing of beauty for Balaam"): the hireling\'s pride — the tape\'s Balaam (Numbers 22:7\'s fees) read back. Fresh.')
srow(250, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"THE LORD WOULD NOT LISTEN TO BALAAM" (23:6) — THE CURSER IS THE CURSED; "HE TURNED THE CURSE TO A BLESSING" — THE CURSER IS CURSED; WHY? "BECAUSE THE LORD YOUR GOD LOVES YOU". ({SP_(250, 5, "שהמקלל", "הוא", "המקלל")} "the curser is the cursed"; {SP_(250, 5, "המקלל", "מתקלל")} "the curser comes to be cursed"; {SP_(250, 5, "כי", "אהבך")} "because He loves you"): 23:6 carries no head — its row inside 250; the reversal of Numbers 23-24 a REFERENCE ROW on the tape\'s own oracles, the love the reason. Fresh.')
srow(251, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SEEK NOT THEIR PEACE NOR THEIR GOOD" (23:7) — SINCE 20:10 SAYS "CALL TO IT FOR PEACE", MIGHT HERE TOO? THE TEACHING SAYS "SEEK NOT THEIR PEACE". The head row of piska 251 — READ BEFORE at chapters 19-21\'s ledger (the peace call\'s exception), REREAD WHOLE here ({SP_(251, 1, "יכול", "אף", "כאן", "כן")} "might here too be so?"; {SP_(251, 1, "לא", "תדרוש", "שלמם")} "seek not their peace"): THE WAR DAEMON\'S PEACE CALL (16b\'s cell) barred for Ammon and Moab — a parameter of the call: no offer to these two; the verse with no kin of two words (find 12). Reread.')
srow(251, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"NOR THEIR GOOD" — SINCE 23:17 SAYS OF THE SLAVE "WHERE IT IS GOOD FOR HIM, OPPRESS HIM NOT", MIGHT HERE TOO? THE TEACHING SAYS "NOR THEIR GOOD". ({SP_(251, 2, "וטובתם")} "nor their good"; {SP_(251, 2, "יכול", "אף", "כאן", "כן")} "might here too be so?"): the slave\'s good (259:6) the foil — Ammon\'s and Moab\'s good not to be sought; the chapter reads itself across ten verses. Fresh.')
srow(251, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"ALL YOUR DAYS FOR EVER" — AND FOR EVERLASTING ETERNITIES. ({SP_(251, 3, "ולעולמי", "עולמים")} "and for everlasting eternities"): the ban\'s duration without end — "for ever" (ad olam, find 8) read as unbounded. Fresh.')
srow(252, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ABHOR NOT AN EDOMITE" (23:8) — WHY? "FOR HE IS YOUR BROTHER", AND BROTHERHOOD IS GREAT. The head row of piska 252 ({SP_(252, 1, "מפני", "מה")} "why?"; {SP_(252, 1, "וגדולה", "אחוה")} "and brotherhood is great"): Esau\'s line the brother (the tape\'s Genesis 25-36) — the reason the status\'s ground. Fresh.')
srow(252, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"ABHOR NOT AN EGYPTIAN" — WHY? "FOR YOU WERE A SOJOURNER IN HIS LAND". R. ELAZAR B. AZARIAH: EGYPT RECEIVED ISRAEL ONLY FOR ITS OWN NEED, AND THE OMNIPRESENT FIXED THEM A REWARD — AN A FORTIORI: IF ONE WHO MEANT NO MERIT AND MERITED IS COUNTED AS MERITING, HOW MUCH MORE ONE WHO MEANS IT. ({SP_(252, 2, "אלא", "לצרך", "עצמם")} "only for their own need"; {SP_(252, 2, "וקבע", "להם", "המקום", "שכר")} "and the Omnipresent fixed them a reward"; {SP_(252, 2, "קל", "וחמר")} "an a fortiori argument"): the unmeant kindness rewarded — the a fortiori named in the Hebrew (kal va-chomer); Genesis 47\'s Egypt read back. Fresh.')
srow(252, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: EGYPT DROWNED ISRAEL IN THE WATER AND EDOM MET THEM WITH THE SWORD — YET BANNED ONLY THREE GENERATIONS; AMMON AND MOAB, WHO TOOK COUNSEL TO MAKE ISRAEL SIN — BANNED FOR EVER: HE WHO MAKES A MAN SIN IS WORSE THAN HIS KILLER, WHO TAKES HIM FROM THIS WORLD ALONE. ({SP_(252, 3, "טבעו", "את", "ישראל", "במים")} "drowned Israel in the water"; {SP_(252, 3, "עד", "שלשה", "דורות")} "up to three generations"; {SP_(252, 3, "אסור", "עולם")} "a ban for ever"; {SP_(252, 3, "שהמחטיא", "את", "האדם", "קשה", "לו", "מן", "ההורגו")} "he who makes a man sin is worse for him than his killer"): THE TWO DURATIONS RANKED — the three generations (23:9) against for ever (23:4) by the gravity of the deed; the world to come named. Fresh.')
srow(253, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SONS" (23:9) — SONS AND NOT DAUGHTERS: R. SHIMON; THE SAGES: "BORN TO THEM" — TO INCLUDE THE DAUGHTERS. The head row of piska 253 ({SP_(253, 1, "בנים", "ולא", "בנות")} "sons and not daughters"; {SP_(253, 1, "לרבות", "את", "הבנות")} "to include the daughters"): the sex parameter again, disputed for Edom and Egypt (Yevamot 8:3 the English\'s "cf."). Fresh.')
srow(253, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: AN A FORTIORI — WHERE MALES ARE BANNED FOR EVER THE FEMALES ENTER AT ONCE; WHERE MALES ARE BANNED THREE GENERATIONS, SHOULD NOT THE FEMALES ENTER AT ONCE? THEY SAID: IF A TRADITION, WE ACCEPT; IF AN ARGUMENT, THERE IS AN ANSWER. HE SAID: I STATE A TRADITION AND SCRIPTURE SUPPORTS ME — "SONS" NOT DAUGHTERS. ({SP_(253, 2, "קל", "וחמר", "הדברים")} "the matter is an a fortiori"; {SP_(253, 2, "אם", "הלכה", "נקבל")} "if it is a tradition we accept"; {SP_(253, 2, "ואם", "לדין", "יש", "תשובה")} "if an argument, there is an answer"; {SP_(253, 2, "הלכה", "אני", "אומר", "והכתוב", "מסיעני")} "I state a tradition and Scripture supports me"): THE RANK OF TRADITION OVER ARGUMENT stated in the spine\'s own words — Yevamot 8:3\'s row; the compiler\'s note: an a fortiori can be answered, a received rule cannot. Fresh.')
srow(253, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE THIRD GENERATION" — MIGHT THE FIRST AND SECOND BE PERMITTED AND THE THIRD FORBIDDEN? THE TEACHING SAYS "THE THIRD GENERATION SHALL ENTER" — THE FIRST AND SECOND FORBIDDEN, THE THIRD PERMITTED. R. JUDAH: BENJAMIN THE EGYPTIAN PROSELYTE, MY COMPANION AMONG R. AKIVA\'S DISCIPLES, MARRIED A PROSELYTE AND MARRIED HIS SON TO ONE THAT HIS GRANDSON MIGHT ENTER. ({SP_(253, 3, "אמר", "מעתה", "ראשון", "ושני", "אסור", "ושלישי", "מתר")} "say from now: the first and the second forbidden, the third permitted"; {SP_(253, 3, "בנימן", "גר", "מצרי")} "Benjamin the Egyptian proselyte"; {SP_(253, 3, "מתלמידי", "רבי", "עקיבא")} "of R. Akiva\'s disciples"): THE COUNT PARAMETER read as a bound (generations 1-2 out, 3 in — the parser\'s ordinal [3]) and a case lived in Yavneh\'s generation; the Tosefta\'s row the English names. Fresh.')
